1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:01,322
Marcus missed one workout

2
00:00:01,322 --> 00:00:02,320
and declared the whole month

3
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:03,057
a failure.

4
00:00:03,307 --> 00:00:04,503
Every evening, he trained,

5
00:00:04,503 --> 00:00:05,908
coloured one square green,

6
00:00:05,908 --> 00:00:06,941
and admired his perfect

7
00:00:06,941 --> 00:00:07,632
calendar.

8
00:00:08,125 --> 00:00:09,089
Soon, protecting

9
00:00:09,089 --> 00:00:10,064
the streak became more

10
00:00:10,064 --> 00:00:11,579
important than enjoying the routine.

11
00:00:11,898 --> 00:00:12,920
Then a storm flooded the

12
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:13,401
lane.

13
00:00:13,593 --> 00:00:14,922
One square stayed blank.

14
00:00:15,416 --> 00:00:16,658
Marcus rolled up the calendar

15
00:00:16,658 --> 00:00:17,668
and marched his shoes toward the

16
00:00:17,668 --> 00:00:18,173
bin.

17
00:00:18,574 --> 00:00:19,607
Luckily, his neighbour was

18
00:00:19,607 --> 00:00:20,518
building a wall.

19
00:00:20,919 --> 00:00:21,917
Unluckily, Marcus was about

20
00:00:21,917 --> 00:00:23,352
to explain bricks to a bricklayer.

21
00:00:23,543 --> 00:00:24,507
He pointed at one empty

22
00:00:24,507 --> 00:00:25,105
space.

23
00:00:25,424 --> 00:00:26,631
The neighbour looked at the gap,

24
00:00:26,631 --> 00:00:27,700
then at all the bricks still

25
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:28,286
standing.

26
00:00:28,686 --> 00:00:29,766
You see, habits

27
00:00:29,766 --> 00:00:30,730
develop through repetition

28
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:31,978
in a familiar situation.

29
00:00:32,297 --> 00:00:33,377
In one study of everyday

30
00:00:33,377 --> 00:00:34,584
habits, missing a single

31
00:00:34,584 --> 00:00:35,675
opportunity did not materially

32
00:00:35,675 --> 00:00:36,831
disrupt the process.

33
00:00:36,976 --> 00:00:38,108
Think of adding bricks.

34
00:00:38,601 --> 00:00:39,611
Skipping one delivery doesn't

35
00:00:39,611 --> 00:00:41,010
make yesterday's wall disappear.

36
00:00:41,329 --> 00:00:42,456
But abandoning the building site

37
00:00:42,456 --> 00:00:43,808
certainly stops it getting taller.

38
00:00:44,302 --> 00:00:45,718
So the next evening, Marcus

39
00:00:45,718 --> 00:00:46,659
put his shoes beside the same

40
00:00:46,659 --> 00:00:47,820
doorway and returned to his usual

41
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:48,499
routine.

42
00:00:49,108 --> 00:00:50,548
No heroic double session.

43
00:00:50,548 --> 00:00:51,924
Just the next sensible step.

44
00:00:52,324 --> 00:00:53,427
A week later, his calendar

45
00:00:53,427 --> 00:00:54,374
still had a gap.

46
00:00:54,774 --> 00:00:55,738
It also had seven new

47
00:00:55,738 --> 00:00:56,660
green squares.

48
00:00:57,154 --> 00:00:58,141
This time, Marcus used

49
00:00:58,141 --> 00:00:59,528
a brick to hold the calendar flat.

50
00:01:00,021 --> 00:01:01,020
Apparently, progress needed

51
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:02,146
a paperweight more than a perfect

52
00:01:02,146 --> 00:01:02,699
record.
